.TH hlcalc 1 31-JUL-2026 "Kozmix Go"

.SH NAME
hlcalc \- calculate capacitance, resistance and/or cut-off frequency of
high-pass or low-pass filters

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hlcalc
[C=val] [R=val] [F=val]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR hlcalc,
given any two out of capacitance, resistance or cut-off frequency, will
calculate the other two values. You must call
.B hlcalc
with exactly two arguments.

.SH OPTIONS
.B hlcalc
accepts SI prefixes (k, M, μ etc.) as part of its command line
options, which are:

.TP
.B C=val
specify capacitance in Farad
.TP
.B R=val
specify resistance in ohms
.TP
.B F=val
specify frequency in Hertz

.TP
All arguments are case insensitive. The SI prefixes are not.

.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
$ hlcalc  r=1M c=2.2n
resistance   R = 1 MΩ
capacitance  C = 2.2 nF
frequency    F = 72.34 Hz
.EE

.SH AUTHOR
svm
